# a drum step's two strengths on its key: an empty step is set strong (100); pressed again, soft (50);
# again, off. A hit of any velocity over 82 goes to soft, one at 82 or under off; turning a knob while
# held keeps it as turned
wait 200
expect track 0
expect step1 0
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 1
expect vel1 100
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 1
expect vel1 50
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 0
# set, then held and turned up to 127: it stays at 127
tapkey w1
wait 20
key w1 down
wait 20
spin K1 40
key w1 up
wait 20
expect step1 1
expect vel1 127
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect vel1 50
# held and turned down (to 30): let go, it stays; pressed, it goes
key w1 down
wait 20
spin K1 -5
key w1 up
wait 20
expect vel1 30
tapkey w1
wait 20
expect step1 0
expect dropped 0
# on the screen: strong (100), soft (50), and a 64 as older projects kept their soft ones, a shade
# brighter than today's soft
tapkey w1
tapkey w2
tapkey w2
tapkey w3
wait 20
key w3 down
wait 20
spin K1 -9
key w3 up
wait 20
expect vel1 100
expect vel2 50
expect vel3 64
